  {
    "episode_id": 66385,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/6/6/66385.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 3,
    "turn_text": "The country I think is now really clear about the issues related to climate change. And I think also the Democratic caucuses in both the Senate and the House in Congress have been really clear that you need an infrastructure plan. You have to have an aggressive climate change plan and states have been like ours have been tired of waiting for the federal government. So the climate, pardon the pun, forgetting this done is completely different. And the fact that the United States has been identified as a problem as the world tries to attack the climate crisis. Those issues are ever more present. And of course, now with a thousand plus scientists saying, you are out of time. There's no pivoting. There's no building. It has to be this immediate focus. I think all of those give you a whole different context for getting this done.",
